  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4-3x).$\n\n$\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4-3x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{64}-\u22ef$",
  "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of logarithms, we observe that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4-3x) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4(1-\\frac{3x}{4})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4)+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-\\frac{3x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Maclaurin series for $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-\\frac{3x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-\\frac{3x}{4}) & =(-\\frac{3x}{4})-\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{3x}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{(-\\frac{3x}{4})}^{3}-\u22ef \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{16})+\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{27{x}^{3}}{64})-\u22ef \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{32}-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{64}-\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the desired result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4-3x) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4)+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-\\frac{3x}{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4)+(-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{32}-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{64}-\u22ef) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(4)-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{32}-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{64}-\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$",
